      "prompt": "TEXT:\nТурист пришёл вечром.\nPREDICATE:\nпришёл\nTARGET:\nвечером\nCANDIDATE RELATIONS:\nPLACE: TARGET specifies where or to what place the event/participant is located or moves; it is not the origin it comes from\nPREDICATED_STATE: TARGET is a property, condition, class, status, or value predicated of a participant\nTIME_POINT: TARGET locates the event on a timeline and answers when it happens; it does not describe how the event is performed\nELAPSED_DURATION: TARGET specifies the elapsed temporal length of the event/state and answers how long it lasts\nCAUSE: TARGET is the reason or prior circumstance that causes/explains why the event happens\nINTENDED_GOAL: TARGET is the intended goal or result for which the event is performed\nQUANTITY_OR_MEASURE: TARGET specifies quantity, count, size, degree, or non-temporal measure; it is not elapsed duration\nMANNER_OR_PROCEDURE: TARGET describes the manner, procedure, or method by which the event is carried out, rather than naming a separate tool or constituent material; a concrete implement such as a hammer/pencil/key is TOOL\nTRANSITION_OPERATOR: TARGET is not an actant; it explicitly marks that the predicate occurrence begins, ends, continues, repeats, or no longer holds\nQUESTION:\nWhich single relation does TARGET have in this event? Use the whole sentence. Grammatical negation (НЕ) negates the proposition or contrasts a filler; by itself it never changes that filler's semantic role and never means ABSENT_ENTITY. Choose ABSENT_ENTITY only when TARGET itself is explicitly represented as absent/excluded/non-participating. Distinguish AFFECTED_OR_CONTENT from CONSTITUENT_MATERIAL strictly: MATERIAL means TARGET is a substance/component incorporated into a different affected or resulting entity; if TARGET is itself the affected/content/result entity, it is not MATERIAL. Choose only among the listed candidate relations.\nCHOICES:\nPLACE\nPREDICATED_STATE\nTIME_POINT\nELAPSED_DURATION\nCAUSE\nINTENDED_GOAL\nQUANTITY_OR_MEASURE\nMANNER_OR_PROCEDURE\nTRANSITION_OPERATOR\n\nTASK:\nChoose one label from CHOICES for TARGET's semantic relation to PREDICATE. Use the whole sentence. Negation of an event or contrastive filler does not change TARGET's role and does not imply ABSENT_ENTITY. Use ABSENT_ENTITY only when TARGET itself is absent, excluded, or non-participating. Return only the label.",
